The code statements that lead to the bug are:
ret = __sev_do_cmd_locked(SEV_CMD_PEK_CSR, &data, &argp->error);
input.length = data.len;
if (blob) {
	if (copy_to_user(input_address, blob, input.length))
		ret = -EFAULT;
}
Reason:
When the firmware command fails (e.g., due to an insufficient buffer size), `data.len` may be set to the required length, which can exceed the allocated `blob` size. The code then copies this oversized length to userspace and attempts to copy a blob of that size from the kernel buffer to userspace, causing a slab-out-of-bounds read and potential data leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (ret || WARN_ON_ONCE(argp->error))
	goto e_free_blob;
Reason:
By checking the return value and firmware error code before the blob copy, the fix ensures that if the command failed, the copy is skipped entirely. This prevents the out-of-bounds read and data leak, while still returning the required length to userspace for proper retry.

